  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nYou must perform the following operation **exactly** KKK times:\n\n\nChoose two distinct indices iii and jjj (1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\leq N1≤i&lt;j≤N).\nThen,\n\nIf (Ai+Aj)(A_i + A_{j})(Ai​+Aj​) is even, append Ai+Aj2\\frac{A_i + A_{j}}{2}2Ai​+Aj​​ to AAA.\nIf (Ai+Aj)(A_i + A_{j})(Ai​+Aj​) is odd, append Ai+Aj+12\\frac{A_i + A_{j} + 1}{2}2Ai​+Aj​+1​ to AAA.\n\n\nNNN is increased by 111 after this.\nFind the minimum possible sum of the final array, after performing this operation KKK times.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the length of the array and the number of times the operation must be performed.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible sum of the array after KKK operations.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,K≤1091 \\leq A_i, K \\leq 10^91≤Ai​,K≤109",
      "The sum of NNN across all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5 1\n6 5 7 4 7\n5 2\n1 4 10 8 1",
        "output": "34\n26",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Choose the elements A2=5A_2 = 5A2​=5 and A4=4A_4 = 4A4​=4, to obtain avg(5,4)=5\\text{avg}(5, 4) = 5avg(5,4)=5, and append it to AAA.\nThe array is now [6,5,7,4,7,5][6, 5, 7, 4, 7, 5][6,5,7,4,7,5], with a sum of 343434. This is optimal.\nTest case 222: Two moves need to be performed. In both moves, choose A1=1A_1 = 1A1​=1 and A5=1A_5 = 1A5​=1, which give avg(1,1)=1\\text{avg}(1, 1) = 1avg(1,1)=1.\nThe final array will be [1,4,10,8,1,1,1][1, 4, 10, 8, 1, 1, 1][1,4,10,8,1,1,1] with a sum of 262626, which is optimal."
      }
    ]
